    "message": "fix(mcp): harden the stdio server — line-size cap, tree-kill, protocol-abuse matrix (#219)\n\nByte-bounded line reader replaces readline: a message over 1 MiB is\nrejected with -32700 and the reader resyncs at the next newline, so a\npathological client can never force unbounded buffering.\n\nReject JSON-RPC batches with a single -32600; validate jsonrpc version\nand id type per JSON-RPC 2.0.\n\nKill whole process trees on cancel/timeout/overflow/shutdown: children\nspawn detached (own group on POSIX; taskkill /T on Windows), and the\nexecutor tracks live children for disposeAll() on EOF and SIGINT/SIGTERM,\nso a tool that spawned the indexing backend cannot leak it.\n\n14 new tests: protocol-abuse matrix (oversize, batch, malformed shapes,\nunknown _meta, concurrent cancels, sequential queue, notification storm,\nidempotent initialize, partial frame at EOF) + grandchild reaping and\ndisposeAll() orphan-prevention. Full suite 749 passed / 2 skipped.",
